{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011BC5A2mhxWGG3KYjDifaoR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel01.2\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel01.2 — sponge specification and differential test\"\n     3→release: rel01.2\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel01.2-uc001-sponge\n     7→  - prd007-sponge R1\n     8→  - prd007-sponge R2\n     9→  - prd007-sponge R3\n    10→  - prd007-sponge R4\n    11→  - prd007-sponge R5\n    12→  - prd007-sponge R6\n    13→\n    14→preconditions:\n    15→  - ./bin/sponge exists (built via mage build).\n    16→  - Reference binary sponge is installed via Homebrew (moreutils) and on PATH.\n    17→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/sponge/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    18→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    19→  - \"sponge: each test creates an isolated temp directory. Comparison is on output file content (prd001-testutils R5) for tests with an output filename. Passthrough mode tests compare stdout byte-for-byte.\"\n    20→\n    21→test_cases:\n    22→  - name: sponge_small_stdin_to_file\n    23→    description: 100 lines piped to sponge with an output filename; compare output file content.\n    24→    inputs:\n    25→      args: [\"outfile.txt\"]\n    26→      stdin: \"seq 1 100 output (lines 1 through 100, each followed by newline)\"\n    27→      env: []\n    28→    normalization: none\n    29→    expected:\n    30→      exit_code: 0\n    31→      stdout_structure: 'expected file outfile.txt contains \"100 lines, 1\\n through 100\\n\"'\n    32→      stderr: \"\"\n    33→    traces:\n    34→      - prd007-sponge R1.1\n    35→      - prd007-sponge R1.2\n    36→      - prd007-sponge R2.1\n    37→\n    38→  - name: sponge_soak_before_write\n    39→    description: 'Same input and output file (cat file | sponge file). Output must equal input, proving sponge did not truncate before reading. Setup: data.txt contains \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\", Pipeline: cat data.txt | sponge data.txt'\n    40→    inputs:\n    41→      args: [\"data.txt\"]\n    42→      stdin: \"content of data.txt (fed via 'cat data.txt')\"\n    43→      env: []\n    44→    normalization: none\n    45→    expected:\n    46→      exit_code: 0\n    47→      stdout_structure: 'expected file data.txt contains \"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\"'\n    48→      stderr: \"\"\n    49→    traces:\n    50→      - prd007-sponge R1.1\n    51→      - prd007-sponge R2.5\n    52→\n    53→  - name: sponge_passthrough_stdout\n    54→    description: No output filename; stdin content appears on stdout.\n    55→    inputs:\n    56→      args: []\n    57→      stdin: \"hello world\\n\"\n    58→      env: []\n    59→    normalization: none\n    60→    expected:\n    61→      exit_code: 0\n    62→      stdout: \"hello world\\n\"\n    63→      stderr: \"\"\n    64→    traces:\n    65→      - prd007-sponge R4.1\n    66→      - prd007-sponge R4.3\n    67→\n    68→  - name: sponge_append_mode\n    69→    description: '-a flag prepends original file content before stdin content. Setup: existing.txt contains \"original line\\n\"'\n    70→    inputs:\n    71→      args: [\"-a\", \"existing.txt\"]\n    72→      stdin: \"appended line\\n\"\n    73→      env: []\n    74→    normalization: none\n    75→    expected:\n    76→      exit_code: 0\n    77→      stdout_structure: 'expected file existing.txt contains \"original line\\nappended line\\n\"'\n    78→      stderr: \"\"\n    79→    traces:\n    80→      - prd007-sponge R3.1\n    81→      - prd007-sponge R3.3\n    82→\n    83→  - name: sponge_append_mode_no_existing_file\n    84→    description: '-a with a non-existent output file behaves as default mode (creates new file). Setup: newfile.txt does not exist'\n    85→    inputs:\n    86→      args: [\"-a\", \"newfile.txt\"]\n    87→      stdin: \"new content\\n\"\n    88→      env: []\n    89→    normalization: none\n    90→    expected:\n    91→      exit_code: 0\n    92→      stdout_structure: 'expected file newfile.txt contains \"new content\\n\"'\n    93→      stderr: \"\"\n    94→    traces:\n    95→      - prd007-sponge R3.2\n    96→\n    97→  - name: sponge_large_stdin\n    98→    description: Input >= 1 MB forces temp-file spill; output file content must match.\n    99→    inputs:\n   100→      args: [\"large_out.txt\"]\n   101→      stdin: \"generated payload of 1,048,576+ bytes (e.g., seq 1 50000)\"\n   102→      env: []\n   103→    normalization: none\n   104→    expected:\n   105→      exit_code: 0\n   106→      stdout_structure: 'expected file large_out.txt contains \"identical to stdin content\"'\n   107→      stderr: \"\"\n   108→    traces:\n   109→      - prd007-sponge R1.3\n   110→      - prd007-sponge R1.4\n   111→\n   112→  - name: sponge_output_file_exists_mode\n   113→    description: 'Existing file has mode 0640; after sponge, file mode is preserved. Setup: protected.txt exists with mode 0640 and contains \"old content\\n\"'\n   114→    inputs:\n   115→      args: [\"protected.txt\"]\n   116→      stdin: \"new content\\n\"\n   117→      env: []\n   118→    normalization: none\n   119→    expected:\n   120→      exit_code: 0\n   121→      stdout_structure: 'expected file protected.txt contains \"new content\\n\" with mode 0640'\n   122→      stderr: \"\"\n   123→    traces:\n   124→      - prd007-sponge R2.3\n   125→\n   126→  - name: sponge_empty_stdin\n   127→    description: Zero bytes of stdin; output file created with zero bytes.\n   128→    inputs:\n   129→      args: [\"empty_out.txt\"]\n   130→      stdin: \"\"\n   131→      env: []\n   132→    normalization: none\n   133→    expected:\n   134→      exit_code: 0\n   135→      stdout_structure: 'expected file empty_out.txt contains \"\"'\n   136→      stderr: \"\"\n   137→    traces:\n   138→      - prd007-sponge R1.1\n   139→      - prd007-sponge R2.1\n   140→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UfZRom1wvEkoY4EpTGxoMu","session_id":"4bed78a5-ce10-