{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012A8sipkGeufYJoVLA9sFdM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All acceptance criteria verified:\n\n- **AC1**: `cmd/sponge/main.go` exists and compiles with `go build ./cmd/sponge/`\n- **AC2**: `seq 1 100 | sponge outfile.txt` writes all 100 lines correctly\n- **AC3**: `-a` flag appends stdin after original file content (`original line\\nappended line\\n`)\n- **AC4**: Error conditions produce stderr messages with `sponge:` prefix and exit code 1\n- **AC5**: All PRD requirements implemented:\n  - **R1** (soak-before-write): `cat file | sponge file` preserves content, proving stdin is fully read before output opens. Memory buffer starts at 8192 bytes (R1.2), spills to TMPDIR temp file at 256MB threshold (R1.3, R1.4), signal cleanup registered for SIGINT/SIGTERM/SIGHUP/SIGPIPE (R1.5)\n  - **R2** (output file handling): Atomic rename with cross-device copy fallback (R2.1, R2.2), file permissions preserved via lstat (R2.3, R2.4), no partial-write visibility (R2.5)\n  - **R3** (append mode): Original content prepended before stdin content (R3.1, R3.3), non-existent file behaves as default mode (R3.2)\n  - **R4** (passthrough): No filename writes buffered stdin to stdout (R4.1), handles both spill (R4.2) and in-memory (R4.3) paths\n  - **R5** (exit codes/errors): Exit 0 on success (R5.1), exit 1 with stderr messages on all error paths (R5.2, R5.3), temp files cleaned up on all exit paths (R5.4)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":256,"cache_read_input_tokens":80075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":256},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bed78a5-ce10-4005-a086-7164c95aed1f","uuid":"a3fa218d-a9ba-40ef-b707-b38ece149a61"}
